[LCAP.7.1] Adding a capability requires, together:

1. a member of `proto/capabilities.proto#Capability`, the next unused
   number, and a row in [LCAP.1];
2. the clause specifying it: in [LCAP.2] if it has engine consequences,
   otherwise in [LFCA];
3. its setting in each built-in dialect ([LDIA.9]);
4. any dependency it has, as a fundamental constraint ([LCAP.3.8]);
5. the compiler's gating of the constructs it governs, and its
   contribution to `requires` ([RDSC.16.2.8]);
6. conformance tests: a program using a governed construct under `false`
   fails to compile.

Every integrator dialect definition must then set it, or fail to load
([NDLC.2.2]).

Most new language features are not capabilities: they are part of the
language, available to every program ([LDIA.4.2]).

